From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <mk@verveflux.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Feb 2026 20:35:42 +0530
Subject: Migrate override storage from string key to Symbol key for
 anti-detection

Replace all window.customOverrides (string property) lookups with
window[Symbol.for('__co')] (Symbol property) across the entire override
hook system. Symbol-keyed properties are invisible to
Object.getOwnPropertyNames(window), which bot detection libraries like
FingerprintJS use to enumerate non-standard window properties.

Files changed:
- v8_builtin_overrides.cc: Updated GenericBuiltinWrapper,
  GenericConstructorWrapper, InstallPropertyExistenceOverrides,
  OverridePropertyAccessorGetter, OverrideDataPropertyGetter,
  GenericOverrideOnlyCallback, and all Pattern V/X/Y callbacks
  to use v8::Symbol::For(isolate, "__co") instead of string key
- custom_override_helpers.h: Updated GetCustomOverrideFunction
  shared helper used by all ForBinding pattern (A-G) methods

All 283 override APIs across 20 batches now use the Symbol path.
The preload scripts already use Symbol.for('__co') so this change
makes the C++ side consistent with the JS side.

